## 💡 Architecture & Conceptual Breakdown

Before writing code, let's address your questions regarding **Docker vs. Local Execution** and **Understanding vs. Copy-Pasting**:

### 1. Do we need to setup Docker first or can we use the old one?
> **Answer: We do NOT need Docker for Day 2!**
> - **Day 2 Scope**: In Day 2, we are building and verifying the pure Python ingestion logic (`requests`, token management, 429 backoff, pagination loops). Running locally via `.venv\Scripts\python` is much faster, has zero container overhead, and lets us inspect raw JSON files directly in `data/raw/`.
> - **When Docker Comes In**: Docker & Airflow orchestration come into play on **Day 8 (Airflow Orchestration)** and **Day 10 (Production Containerization & CI/CD)**. When we reach Day 8, we will reuse and adapt the existing `airflow/docker-compose.yaml`.

